  "text_md": "# TRAINING ZONE\n\n![](<74094decfc2f4504fb7e14a3969e2abe71d5eaf9_page_3_images/imageFile1.png>)\n\nYOUR 4-WEEK PLAN\n\nIntermediate/advanced\n\n# BKE TRAINING\n\nRAMPUP YOUR TRAINING INTENSITY WITH THIS FOUR-WEEK CYCLEFITNESS PLAN\n\n![](<74094decfc2f4504fb7e14a3969e2abe71d5eaf9_page_3_images/imageFile2.png>)\n\nFOLD 1\n\n# WEEK 01\n\n# WEEK 02\n\n# Rest day\n\nAMSwim2,5OOm Techniquesession\n\nWU3x300as(IOOmFC, IOOmKICK, IOOmPULL) MAIN8xSOmas (25mFISTS, 25mFC) 3x(150m WD3OOmeasyFCorBACK\n\nPMBike SOmins WUIOminsin Z2MAINIO,9,\n\n# Rest day\n\nAMSwim 2,5OOm Muscular endurancesession +2OsecsRI, 2OOmPULLinZI, IOOmFCinZ3 WDSOOmeasy FCorBACK\n\nPMBike5Omins WUIOminsinZ2\n\nMAIN3,4,5,6,5,4,3minsallinZ3 (+IminRI) WD4minsin Z2\n\nRun 45mins   WU 10mins as (5mins in Z2, 5mins in Z3) MAIN 8x1min flat-out fast (+2 mins jog RI) WD 10mins in Z2\n\nFC, IOOmKICK, 300mPULL,IOOmKICK WD 2OOmeasy FCIBACK PMBike 5Omins WUIOminsas (SminsinZ2, SminsinZ3) MAIN6x3minshardinZ4 (+3minRI\n\ninZI)WDSminsin Z2\n\nRun 40mins WU 12mins as (5mins in Z2, 5mins in Z3, 2mins in Z2) MAIN 5x2mins flat-out fast (+2mins jog recoveries) WD 10mins in Z2\n\nAMSwim2,6OOmStrengthsession WU 2O0m ANKLESin Z2 +3OsecsRIWD4OOmFCIBACKI BREASTPMBike 4Smins WU IOminsas (Smins inZ2, SminsinZ3) MAIN3Ominsas (alternating 2minsinZ4, 2minsinZ2)WDSminsinZ2\n\n5\n\nRun 60mins   WU 25mins in Z2 MAIN 15mins in Z3 WD 20mins in Z2\n\nRun6Omins WU 25minsinZ2\n\nMAIN ISminsinZ3WD 2Ominsin Z2\n\nẵ\n\nBike 2 hour endurance ride in Z2\n\n![](<74094decfc2f4504fb7e14a3969e2abe71d5eaf9_page_3_images/imageFile3.png>)\n\nBike 2 hour endurance ride in Z2\n\nBike 2hr 30mins endurance ride in Z2\n\nBike 2hr 30mins endurance ride in Z2\n\n# TRAINING ZONES\n\nUSING THESE Training Zones will help you train at the right intensity for each session. This helps develop specific aspects of your fitness, as well as making sure you don’t overdo it.\n\nYou can either estimate your intensity using the Training Zone descriptions, or use a heart-rate monitor for a more precise measure. If you use a heart-rate monitor, use the percentages provided and subtract them from your maximum heart rate to calculate your zones. Tools like cycle power meters and GPS watches will also help track your training progress, but they’re not essential for these plans.\n\nThese training zones are only a guide, so don’t worry about being overly precise with heart rates because they’ll fluctuate anyway. It’s good to be mindful of your intensity but it’s even more important that you get out there and enjoy your training.\n\n# ZONE1 [Zl] Recovery\n\nEasy pace, feels nice and light.\n\n![](<74094decfc2f4504fb7e14a3969e2abe71d5eaf9_page_3_images/imageFile5.png>)\n\nZONE 2 [Z2]   Steady 65 to 75% of your maximum. Fairly easy pace. Easy enough so that you could breathe just through your nose if you wanted to.\n\n# ZONE3 [Z3] Tempo\n\nmaximum. A fairly hard but sustainable pace.\n\n# ZONE 4 [Z4] Race tempo\n\nA hard pace that requires real focus to sustain.\n\nKEY WU Warm up, WD Warm down, MAIN Main set, FC Front crawl, KICK Kick with a float held out in front of you, BUILD Gradually increase the intensity of each rep within a set, PULL Front crawl with a pull float between thighs,   RI Rest interval, BACK Backstroke, BREAST Breaststroke, 1-ARM Front crawl using one arm only N/S Negative split – swim the 2nd half faster than the first, FDRAG Drag your fingers along the surface during the FC   arm recovery, FISTS   Swim FC   with clenched fists, DOG Doggy paddle, SCULL Kick with arms held out in front, sculling your hands side to side, BAND Front crawl with a rubber band or inner-tube tied around ankles, ANKLES Front crawl with pull float between ankles\n\n# STAY IN THE TRAINING ZONE WITH   TRIATHLON PLUS\n\n# WEEK 03\n\n# Rest day\n\nAM Swim 2,900m Technique session WU 300m FC, 200m KICK, 200m FC MAIN 3 x (300m PULL in Z3 +30secs RI, 100m FC in Z2 +20secs RI, 100secs FC in Z3 +20secs RI, 100m FC in Z4 +20secs RI) WD 400m easy FC or BACK PM   Bike 50mins   WU 10mins in Z2 MAIN 10,9, 8mins all in Z3 (+90secs RI) WD 10mins in Z2\n\n# WEEK 04\n\n# Rest day\n\nAMSwim2 OOOm Techniquesession WU3OOmFC; 2OOmKICK, IOOmPULL +2Osecs WD2OOmeasy FCorBACK PMBike 4Smins WUISminsas IOminsinZ2, alternating (3Osecsmax, 3Osecsrecovery spin)\n\n3minsinZ3,2minsin Z2MAIN 2Ominsas WDIOminsinZ2\n\nRun 40mins   WU 15mins as (10mins in Z2, 5mins in Z3) MAIN 4x3mins flat-out fast (+2mins jog recoveries) WD 8mins in Z2\n\nSmins\n\nAM Swim 2,500m Strength session WU 2x250m FC, 100m KICK, 200m PULL MAIN 8x(25m SCULL, 25m FC)+10secs RI, 100m PULL in Z4 +10secs RI, 200m FC in Z3 +10secs RI, 300m PULL in Z2 +30secs RI, 200m FC in Z3 +20secs RI, 100m FC in Z4 WD 400m FC in Z1   PM   Bike 45mins   WU 10mins as (5mins in Z2, 5mins in Z3) MAIN 30mins as (alternating 2mins in Z4, 2mins in Z2) WD 5mins in Z2\n\nAM Swim 2,300m Strength session WU 200m FC, 100m KICK, 200m PULL, 100m FC MAIN 400m (alternating 50m FC, 25m KICK). 3x (200m PULL, 100m KICK in Z3) +30secs RI WD 400m BACK/BREAST PM   Bike 45mins   WU 15mins as 10mins in Z2, 3mins in Z3, 2mins in Z2 MAIN 20mins as alternating (30secs max, 30secs recovery spin) WD 10mins in Z2\n\nWDIOminsinZ2\n\n5\n\nRun 60mins   WU 25mins in Z2 MAIN 15mins in Z3 WD 20mins in Z2\n\nRun 40mins   WU 15mins in Z2 MAIN 15mins in Z3 WD 10mins in Z2\n\nẵ\n\nẵ\n\nBike 3 hour endurance ride in Z2\n\nBike 2 hour endurance ride in Z2\n\nBike 2 hour endurance ride in Z2\n\nBike 2 hour endurance ride in Z2\n\ntriradarcom\n\n![](<74094decfc2f4504fb7e14a3969e2abe71d5eaf9_page_3_images/imageFile4.png>)\n\n",
